Tested source: `rust-v0.163.0`, commit `83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012`, Windows x64. The same reservation path was also observed in inspected main commit `6b991972c5b539198dcea9bac4fc14e57559c3af`.

`Config::effective_agent_max_threads(V2)` subtracts one for the root. `is_v2_resident_session_source` classifies only `SessionSource::SubAgent` as resident candidates. However, `ensure_v2_agent_loaded` unconditionally reserves and commits a child residency slot when reloading any thread, including the root.

Reproduction uses the real `codex-core` controller fixture and dummy test credentials, with no model inference:

1. Configure total capacity as four and create a root with three children.
2. Persist the threads and hold child residency pins so no worker can be evicted.
3. Shut down and remove only the root runtime.
4. Send queue-only mail from a surviving child to that root.

Original result: `AgentLimitReached { max_threads: 3 }`. The equivalent capacity-two case fails with `max_threads: 1`. Both regression cases failed at the root-message send as expected.

Expected: the root reloads and receives the queued message while all child runtimes remain unchanged. Nested parents that are themselves SubAgents must still use residency capacity.

Proposed fix: make reservation and commit conditional on the existing `is_v2_resident_session_source` predicate. Do not increase limits, disable agents, evict active children, or suppress errors.

Patched test result: both regression cases passed. Seven existing related cases also passed: shared instructions after root unload (3), evicted nested-parent authority (1), cancelled-send reload registration (1), and residency unit tests (2).

Full executable comparison is now verified as well. A local scripted Responses server drives real `app-server --stdio` instances in isolated temporary homes; no external model inference is used. With `[features.multi_agent_v2] enabled = true` and `max_concurrent_threads_per_session = 4`, three child requests remain active while the completed root is unloaded using `thread/unsubscribe`. The loaded-thread list changes from root plus three children to only those same three children. A child then sends queue-only mail to `/root` through the real collaboration tool.

- Official 0.163.0: `collab tool failed: agent thread limit reached`; the root remains unloaded.
- Patched optimized release build: send succeeds, the root reloads, and all three child IDs remain loaded. After a parent tool-processing step, the subsequent parent model request contains the queued agent message with the expected sender, recipient and fixture sentinel. The parent turn completes.
- Both isolated app-server processes exit successfully. The patched build also passes actual Node MCP execution and a protected workspace-write shell probe.

This is targeted core and app-server coverage, not a full suite or Desktop UI end-to-end validation. The installed application has not been replaced; production auto-updates remain enabled.

Related but different: #34518 and #32353 concern completed children retaining capacity through mailbox state. This case concerns a root reload incorrectly requesting capacity reserved for children.

